# 2. User Roles & Permissions

Create four main user roles.

### A. Super Admin

The Super Admin can:

- Access the entire application.
- View all campaigns.
- View all imported data.
- View all employees.
- View all data assignments.
- View every employee's activities.
- View all appointments.
- View all reports.
- Manage campaign assignments.
- Manage data managers, HR and sales representatives.
- Configure application settings.
- View the complete company-wide performance dashboard.
- Monitor data duplication and distribution.
- View all historical activities and audit logs.

### B. Data Manager

The Data Manager is responsible for preparing and distributing prospecting data.

Permissions:

- Import company and contact datasets.
- Upload Excel and CSV files.
- Create campaigns.
- Manage campaigns assigned to them.
- Review imported records.
- Clean and validate records.
- Use AI-based data scoring fields if available.
- Categorize data.
- Identify duplicate companies and contacts.
- Request or assign data to sales representatives.
- Monitor how much data has been distributed.
- View which records have been worked on.
- View unworked records.
- Request additional data.
- Manage campaign data allocations.

Data managers should not have access to restricted admin functions such as employee password management, system settings or full company administration.

### C. HR Manager

HR should be able to:

- Create new employee accounts.
- Create sales representative accounts.
- Create data manager accounts.
- Create manager accounts.
- Assign employee roles.
- Activate and deactivate employees.
- Reset passwords.
- View employee profiles.
- View employee joining dates.
- Assign departments.
- Maintain employee details.
- Track leave requests if a leave module is available.
- Assign training and company policies if an HR module is added later.

HR should be able to manage employees without accessing restricted sales data unless specifically granted permission.

### D. Sales Representative / Prospecting Executive

Sales representatives should:

- Log in to their own account.
- See only the companies and contacts assigned to them.
- See their assigned campaigns.
- See records that have not yet been worked on.
- See their previously worked records.
- View company websites.
- View LinkedIn company and prospect profile links.
- Record calls, emails, LinkedIn outreach and WhatsApp outreach activities.
- Record outcomes.
- Add remarks and notes.
- Create follow-up reminders.
- Schedule appointments.
- View their own performance.
- Request additional prospecting data.
- View their own follow-up tasks.
- View their appointment calendar.

Sales representatives must not see records assigned to other representatives unless explicitly permitted by their manager.

