## Duplicate Prevention System

This is one of the most important features.

The application must prevent the same company or contact from being distributed multiple times unnecessarily.

Create duplicate detection based on:

- Normalized company domain.
- Company website.
- Company name.
- Contact email.
- Contact LinkedIn profile URL.
- Contact phone number.
- Normalized company/contact identifiers.

Create a centralized company and contact database.

A company should not be treated as a new company just because it appears in a different Excel file.

When duplicate records are detected:

- Show the existing record.
- Show the previous campaigns associated with it.
- Show previous assigned sales representatives.
- Show previous outreach history.
- Show previous campaign results.
- Allow the data manager to decide whether the record can be reused in a new campaign based on permissions and campaign rules.

Create a duplicate warning before distribution.

Maintain a complete history of every company and contact.

