# 21. Important Workflow

The system must support this complete operational workflow:

Step 1: Data manager imports companies and contacts from Apollo, Excel or CSV.

Step 2: System validates and cleans data.

Step 3: System identifies duplicates using company domain, email, LinkedIn URLs and other identifiers.

Step 4: Data manager reviews the dataset and assigns it to a campaign.

Step 5: Admin or campaign manager creates the campaign and defines its instructions and qualification criteria.

Step 6: Data manager distributes data to sales representatives.

Step 7: Sales representatives log in and view only their assigned data.

Step 8: Sales representatives research the company and contact.

Step 9: Sales representatives call, email, WhatsApp or perform LinkedIn outreach.

Step 10: Sales representatives record outreach activity, response, outcome and remarks.

Step 11: If a prospect asks for a follow-up, the representative creates a follow-up task.

Step 12: If a prospect agrees to a meeting, the representative creates an appointment.

Step 13: Admin monitors campaigns, assignments, activities, follow-ups, appointments and employee performance.

Step 14: HR creates and manages employee accounts.

Step 15: Sales representatives request additional data when their assigned data is insufficient.

Step 16: Data managers review and fulfil requests.

Step 17: Admin reviews reports and campaign performance.

